        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: तोलणे",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तोलणे — tolṇe — \"to weigh up\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "निर्णय घेण्यापूर्वी त्याने दोन्ही बाजू तोलल्या. nirṇay gheṇyāpūrvī tyāne donhī bājū tolalyā. Before deciding, he weighed up both sides."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with -ने (he …): त्याने तोललं, tyāne tollaṁ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also to weigh on scales."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तोलणे (tolṇe) is inherited: CDIAL lists Marathi tol, \"a weight for weighing\", under Sanskrit tōlya, \"to be weighed\" (CDIAL 5980), and the verb is built on that noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
